WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.750
When Elon Musk has any news to share, you’re
likely to hear about it first on Twitter.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.719
You’d think the guy who runs SpaceX, Neuralink,
Tesla, The Boring Company wouldn’t have

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:10.919
much time on his hands.

00:00:10.919 --> 00:00:14.400
But as his companies grow, so do his number
of tweets.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.590
They’ve been increasing steadily - as the
Wall Street Journal notes in this graphic.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.760
His tweets are so frequent that when he announced
he was taking a break from Twitter that one

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.430
time, it made the news.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:30.060
Ever since he opened up an account in 2009,
he’s tweeted about 16,000 times.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.980
Other famous billionaires tweet far less.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.290
Bill Gates has sent 3,000 tweets.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.750
Jeff Bezos less than 300.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.900
This is said to be Mark Zuckerberg’s account
which isn’t even verified.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.180
He’s sent 19 tweets.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.510
Musk insists Twitter only takes up a “tiny”
bit of his day.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:50.080
And says his tweets are “literally what
I’m thinking at the moment, not carefully

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.950
crafted corporate bs.”

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.430
So, why does he tweet so much?

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:58.730
It’s partly because Tesla dissolved its
public relations team in North America a few

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.890
years back, so Musk IS the PR team.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.820
He breaks news on Twitter about his companies
and responds to journalists.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:10.000
Tesla doesn’t run any commercials so Musk’s
Twitter acts as the advertising department.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.930
However, there’s another reason he tweets
so much.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.940
Musk once said: “I use my tweets to express
myself.”

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.790
He said some people use their hair.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.050
He uses Twitter.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:23.909
And by connecting with people, it gives his
fans and his customers a voice.

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:28.560
It’s the reason most of his tweets are replies,
according to The Wall Street Journal.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.340
For example, when a Twitter user asked if
Tesla could program the cars to move back

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.500
the seat once the car is in park

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.930
Musk responded that it was a good point and
it would be added in one of the software updates.

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:42.910
He’s talked openly about the importance
of feedback, once saying:

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.560
“Seek negative feedback from all corners.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.100
From customers, from people who aren’t customers.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.050
How can we make this better?”

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:52.730
Better products make his companies more successful.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:57.330
Plus, when he responds directly to everyday
followers, it has the added effect of blowing

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:00.330
up on Twitter as people are happy he’s replied
to them.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:03.450
That’s an incredibly powerful connection
to make.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.080
It shows the man cares.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.599
A famous recent example of connecting with
the public is when he asked his 63 million

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:13.040
Twitter followers whether he should sell some
of his Tesla shares.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:18.040
He tweeted: “Much is made lately of unrealized
gains being a means of tax avoidance, so I

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.659
propose selling 10% of my Tesla stock”.

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:24.969
And he said he’d abide by the outcome of
the poll - which was to sell.

00:02:24.969 --> 00:02:29.760
He was likely to do it anyway because of a
multi-billion dollar looming tax bill on expiring

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.120
stock options.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.650
But his poll shows how he cleverly engages
with the public.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.510
Though not everyone was happy.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:40.069
Democratic senator Ron Wyden doesn’t think
Musk is going far enough.

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:42.900
He’s been pushing for new taxes on billionaires.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.169
When Wyden made it known he wasn’t pleased
with the poll, Musk responded:

00:02:46.169 --> 00:02:50.280
“Why does your profile picture look like
you just came?”

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.520
Musk has been known to be casual and sometimes
crude with his comments.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.019
And depending on whose side you’re own,
you either love it or hate it.

00:02:58.019 --> 00:03:02.709
Like the time he tweeted Jeff Bezos “Can’t
get it up (to orbit)” in reference to Bezos’

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:04.629
rocket company Blue Origin.

00:03:04.629 --> 00:03:08.269
Bezos has repeatedly been the victim of his
trolling.

00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:12.540
When the Amazon founder tweeted about how
others thought the online retailer would bomb

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:17.640
in the early days but proved its doubters
wrong, Musk replied with an emoji of a silver

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:18.640
medal.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.980
Implying he was in first place.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:24.909
His reply, by the way, got more likes than
Bezos’ original tweet!

00:03:24.909 --> 00:03:29.090
Musk has said he thinks he’s funny and admits
that his humor gets his companies free publicity.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:33.969
He’s said: “If we are entertaining people,
they (as in the media) would write stories

00:03:33.969 --> 00:03:39.079
about us and we don’t have to spend on advertising
which would reduce the price of our cars.”

00:03:39.079 --> 00:03:43.260
According to Social Blade, a website that
tracks social media stats, his social media

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.590
grade is A++.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:50.030
He even has more followers than some leading
automotive companies combined.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:55.519
His influence can be seen by how he literally
moves markets with the rise and fall of 280

00:03:55.519 --> 00:03:56.519
characters.

00:03:56.519 --> 00:04:00.699
Like when he sent the price of Tesla stock
up 10% when he said he was thinking about

00:04:00.699 --> 00:04:04.640
taking the company private and that funding
was already in place.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:09.629
The SEC charged him with fraud as the transaction
was still uncertain and ordered his future

00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:12.370
tweets to be pre-approved by company lawyers.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:16.400
The Commission then took issue with his tweet
that “Tesla’s stock price is too high

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.840
in my opinion.”

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:22.889
That very day, Tesla’s stock price closed
10% lower than the day before.

00:04:22.889 --> 00:04:26.979
His influence can also be seen by how he moves
the crypto market.

00:04:26.979 --> 00:04:31.069
When he said Tesla would no longer accept
Bitcoin as payment due to the heavy energy

00:04:31.069 --> 00:04:35.979
use of Bitcoin mining, the price of the cryptocurrency
dropped around 15%!

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:41.190
And when he clarified that Tesla would eventually
allow Bitcoin transactions if environmental

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.940
concerns are addressed, the price shot up
10%.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.069
Same thing happened with Dogecoin.

00:04:47.069 --> 00:04:52.009
He sent it up 30% in May after tweeting he
was working with developers to make it more

00:04:52.009 --> 00:04:53.129
efficient.

00:04:53.129 --> 00:04:58.020
Musk appears to have a special place in his
heart for Dogecoin, sharing a "Lion King"-inspired

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:03.080
meme featuring an edited image of him raising
the dogecoin’s Shiba Inu in the air

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.090
before getting a real-life Shiba Inu puppy
himself, Floki.

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:08.570
He is the king of memes.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.349
In his words: “Who controls the memes, controls
the Universe.”

00:05:12.349 --> 00:05:17.669
Or perhaps a better phrase could be: Whoever
controls social media controls the universe.

00:05:17.669 --> 00:05:20.270
He’s not only a master marketer.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.650
Musk says he spends most of his time on engineering.

